    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.basics, mini.move\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nWhen doing an checkhealth on neovim 0.11 I get the following warning:\n\n==============================================================================\nvim.deprecated:                       require(\"vim.deprecated.health\").check()\n\n ~\n- WARNING vim.highlight is deprecated. Feature will be removed in Nvim 2.0.0\n  - ADVICE:\n    - use vim.hl instead.\n    - stack traceback:\n        /home/gael/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/basics.lua:716\n        [C]:-1\n        vim/_editor.lua:0\n        /home/gael/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/move.lua:473\n        /home/gael/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/move.lua:354\n        lua:1\n\n### Reproduction\nmini.move or mini.basics need to be loaded:\n:checkhealth\n",
