            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nYes, 'mini.basics' uses `vim.highlight.on_yank()`. Although this is not breaking anything (at least until Neovim 2.0, which is years away), updating it to possibly use `vim.hl` is still good idea.\n\nI don't think 'mini.move' can provide such warning as it doesn't use `vim.highlight`. There are other modules, though which can be updated. I'll take a look.",
